{number: 106}
{title: Blest Be the Tie}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Blest be the [G7] tie that [C] binds
Our [F] hearts in [C] Christian [G7] love;
The [C] fellowship of [F] kindred [C] minds
Is [F] like to [C] that a-[G7] [C] bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Be-[C] fore our [G7] Father's [C] throne
We [F] pour our [C] ardent [G7] prayers;
Our [C] fears, our hopes, our [F] aims are [C] one,
Our [F] comforts [C] and our [G7] [C] cares.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
We [C] share our [G7] mutual [C] woes,
Our [F] mutual [C] burdens [G7] bear;
And [C] often for each [F] other [C] flows
The [F] sympa-[C] thizing [G7] [C] tear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [C] we a-[G7] sunder [C] part,
It [F] gives us [C] inward [G7] pain;
But [C] we shall still be [F] joined in [C] heart,
And [F] hope to [C] meet a-[G7] [C] gain.
{end_of_verse}
